{"decision":"PROPOSE","invalid_operation":null,"observations":["The expression is a nested product/sum of the form 3(1+3(1+3(...))).","The nesting depth is determined by the number of '3(1+' layers; here there are 10 factors of 3 and 9 inner additions plus the innermost 1.","A deterministic evaluation can be done by iterating from the innermost value outward: start with the innermost constant, then repeatedly apply x -> 3*(1+x).","The general computation is parameterized by the outer multiplier, the additive constant, the innermost seed, and the nesting depth."],"parameter_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"addend":{"description":"The repeated additive constant b inside each layer.","type":"integer"},"depth":{"description":"Number of nested layers a*(b + ...) applied around the seed.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"multiplier":{"description":"The repeated multiplicative factor a in each layer a*(b + ...).","type":"integer"},"seed":{"description":"The innermost constant c at the center of the nesting.","type":"integer"}},"required":["multiplier","addend","seed","depth"],"type":"object"},"procedure_plan":"Parse the source expression into parameters: multiplier a (the repeated factor), additive constant b (the repeated added term), innermost seed c, and nesting depth n (number of times the layer a*(b + ...) is applied). Evaluate by setting x = c, then for i = 1..n: x = a*(b + x). Return x as an exact integer. For the given source, a=3, b=1, c=1, n=10, yielding the nested expression 3(1+3(1+...3(1+1)...)) with 10 layers.","replacement_operation":null,"source_parameters":{"addend":1,"depth":10,"multiplier":3,"seed":1},"uncertainty":"The main ambiguity is counting the nesting depth from the textual expression; the plan assumes the depth equals the number of repeated '3(1+' layers, which must be parsed carefully. Arithmetic is exact and deterministic once parameters are fixed."}